# The eight-bit shift produces 0xB0.
# Reference: (bit<8>) (bit<4>) ((bit<8>) (0xAB << 4) >> offset).
# Offset zero selects only zero-filled bits.
packet 0 AB 00 FF
expect 0 AB 00 00

# Offsets below four select both zero-filled bits and data.
packet 0 AB 01 FF
expect 0 AB 01 08
packet 0 AB 02 FF
expect 0 AB 02 0C
packet 0 AB 03 FF
expect 0 AB 03 06

# Offset four selects only data from the original value.
packet 0 AB 04 FF
expect 0 AB 04 0B

# Slices crossing the upper boundary are zero-extended.
packet 0 AB 05 FF
expect 0 AB 05 05
packet 0 AB 06 FF
expect 0 AB 06 02
packet 0 AB 07 FF
expect 0 AB 07 01

# A slice starting at the value's width is entirely zero.
packet 0 AB 08 FF
expect 0 AB 08 00
